From 58b0fabcd85d2d362d12da3888ff5f3588dd49d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:49:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(allwinner): restart the watchdog counter on system reset

The system reset only switches the watchdog to its shortest interval.
When the OS has left the watchdog running with a longer one, e.g. Linux
with a watchdog daemon on a panic or sysrq reset, the counter is already
past 0.5 seconds and the reset never fires: "PSCI: System reset failed"
and the system hangs until power cycled. Restart the counter as well.

Seen on an A133 (TrimUI Smart Pro), and reproduced from Linux by writing
the same configuration over a running 16 s watchdog: no reset until the
counter was restarted.

Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
index 28abd3c..53e8248 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
+++ b/plat/allwinner/common/sunxi_native_pm.c
@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@ static void __dead2 sunxi_system_reset(void)
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CFG_REG, 1);
 	/* Enable the watchdog with the shortest timeout (0.5 seconds) */
 	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_MODE_REG, (0 << 4) | 1);
+	/*
+	 * Restart the counter: if the OS left the watchdog running with a
+	 * longer timeout, its counter is already past the new one and the
+	 * reset would never happen.
+	 */
+	mmio_write_32(SUNXI_WDOG0_CTRL_REG, (0xa57 << 1) | 1);
 	/* Wait for twice the watchdog timeout before panicking */
 	mdelay(1000);
 
